{"title":"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(Doesn’t_require_good_diagram)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(Doesn’t require good diagram)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Sal_Khan\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Sal Khan</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95fdfbb0362c49460ab4b7ef61acc59d3b0fac79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69bbae25a18275c119a43ad358648ad91674f4e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 13,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/143c2eba1879be818d2435ed05ec1f3cd77139e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 14,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac3d07bc0b103aa9036bce7eb60351c76d01726.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 15,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the intersection of the medians. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/9205b8264f75efd0b832d4d5021d9ad1c5af2b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49de1d8967fe753bab5f2ad2334186448af5a481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6cbc45cd93a2b17b17a9d035a45847271b55322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> are the images of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1e22fe09c7388d738ebd1e52fb999e0eae620f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccedc2f7ab3f66b36d3e0cf1536a3c801f01f421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737b15f20e17e7834a83b8188337bade510f22f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> respectively, after a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> rotation about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e037912024535666d4f5194dcf67a6231061c8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> What is the area of the union of the two regions enclosed by the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366b832e4e0ae724dc7c057a10d7aa073a7cf26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;?$\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/20697823da9ea9148dbc3b247e1758c6baa01188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13-14-15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> triangle is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c1645fea006e40422df8465ad25c74bc33e615eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-12-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> triangle and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a69890fe7f8a233e9346bc908b99d65d084274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-12-15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> triangle \"glued\" together on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> side, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c23eb021f542e6ca0c51b59e044a8d72a3644a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot12\\cdot14=84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"195\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>There are six points of intersection between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac7b44ed04bbe9deaace132f0f977b2c679f134c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />. Connect each of these points to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5d42315a7709b2d03b4403cc072e4b6c1a6fd51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(8cm); pair A,B,C,G,D,E,F,A_1,A_2,B_1,B_2,C_1,C_2; B=(0,0); A=(5,12); C=(14,0); E=(12.6667,8); D=(7.6667,-4); F=(-1.3333,8); G=(6.3333,4); B_1=(4.6667,0); B_2=(1.6667,4); A_1=(3.3333,8); A_2=(8,8); C_1=(11,4); C_2=(9.3333,0); dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(G); dot(D); dot(E); dot(F); dot(A_1); dot(B_1); dot(C_1); dot(A_2); dot(B_2); dot(C_2); draw(B--A--C--cycle); draw(E--D--F--cycle); draw(B_1--A_2); draw(A_1--C_2); draw(C_1--B_2); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,WSW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,ESE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,S); label(&quot;$B&#39;$&quot;,E,ENE); label(&quot;$A&#39;$&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;$C&#39;$&quot;,F,WNW); [/asy]\" width=\"372\" height=\"378\" />\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> smaller congruent triangles which make up the desired area. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is made up of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of such triangles. \nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6302862d09f736b0fabb7cb16d47f75107fba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[\\Delta ABC \\bigcup \\Delta A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;\\right] = \\frac{12}{9}[\\Delta ABC]= \\frac{4}{3}\\cdot84=\\boxed{112}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"418\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.28Doesn.E2.80.99t_require_good_diagram.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(Doesn’t_require_good_diagram)\">Solution 2(Doesn’t require good diagram)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(Doesn’t require good diagram)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> either like the first solution or by using Heron’s Formula. Then, draw the medians from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0bba211f39c1aa42de898401f037d5f302aa617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C, A’, B’,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb2f0e8712221633a9f50d2a9db3db37d8b571d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C’$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Since the medians of a triangle divide the triangle into 6 triangles with equal area, we can find that each of the 6 outer triangles have equal area. (Proof: Since I’m too lazy to draw out a diagram, I’ll just have you borrow the one above. Draw medians <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35ebcd881abc07ce36dce8a81c871f8445a3ea0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a32cdcb1dd53e7f04dffc65d587cc1b40663096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GB’$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and let’s call the points that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35ebcd881abc07ce36dce8a81c871f8445a3ea0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cc50afefbfc3d5bf4eff1cd8b900ef943581d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C’B’$\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> “<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />” and the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a32cdcb1dd53e7f04dffc65d587cc1b40663096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GB’$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> “<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />”. From the previous property and the fact that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2ccbe3e0bae6683fdce8c144467ed9eee274efe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta A’B’C’$\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> are congruent, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c0587858dbf493d3b0e29212cbc6d1ed70632fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta GHB’$\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> has the same area as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05a511dc18e3d45e5d2577046c01ff2075bb8317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta GIA$\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. Because of that, both “half” triangles created also have the same area. The same logic can be applied to all other triangles).\nAlso, since the centroid of a triangle divides each median with the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3714d1977e2e6fa2c03536bd04eabab371fd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, along with the previous fact, each outer triangle has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3dba22edcee4ff7213635505e90128beebb42e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2ccbe3e0bae6683fdce8c144467ed9eee274efe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta A’B’C’$\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the area of the region required is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33bd495b7492f95385da7afb197cd34638cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> times the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7da62d7b3420570b26fd26dd9442ba12a74ef1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {112}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by Someonenumber011\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Rigorous)\">Solution 3 (Rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d33cc80fa8f093e155c5be46d2e5d9da3d7e1ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> can be calculated as 84 using Heron's formula or other methods. Since a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> rotation is equivalent to reflection through a point, we have a homothety with scale factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022948689ac03ea1705a6af78b86d32ae2a369eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> through the centroid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> which maps to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b4f897205beb16e266ea66d8ae8ece27cf5af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M&#39;$\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" /> and note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcd5df2a0addc2e42add99fa13fd5d474194d294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;G=AG=2GM,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"155\" height=\"17\" /> implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecdc0f9a8e7940452ffe2c060d56295949185f4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM=MA&#39;.$\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" /> Similarly, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06f72324c78fa2c159d4ff8c9a34423b2e7fd214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM&#39;=M&#39;G=GM=MA&#39;.$\" width=\"224\" height=\"14\" /> Also let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/3/4e39919f572d9421d9fe01d80321554dfafdeced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;$\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10ab60705bca2b802f4a734cc94fa07aab62e22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;C&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> respectively. The homothety implies that we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b202f6b1784b669ccafe3f5222c5c532c925fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE || B&#39;C&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> so there is in fact another homothety centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d290cc9b82907ed05bbd328c8f485b841d7f0603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;DE$\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022948689ac03ea1705a6af78b86d32ae2a369eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd74e9ae587d8117d5a70835031cebbc1f3e253a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;M&#39;=3A&#39;M,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" /> the scale factor of this homothety is 3 and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8c5ad4f255497451d1ec6be78c0d3f5eaf2979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[A&#39;DE]=\\frac{1}{9}[A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;]=\\frac{1}{9}[ABC].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"256\" height=\"37\" /> We can apply similar reasoning to the other small triangles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022948689ac03ea1705a6af78b86d32ae2a369eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> not contained within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, so our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf265f3f39dca0634609c5edc1c8780de16d37d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]+3\\cdot\\frac{1}{9}[ABC]=\\boxed{112.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"231\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We determine the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> to be 84 via Heron's Formulae. A \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> rotation\" is the same as just reflecting the figure by centroid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Also, a rotation (or reflection by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), simply forms a new triangle that is exactly congruent through SSS to the original. We have established <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022948689ac03ea1705a6af78b86d32ae2a369eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> are congruent.\n</p><p>Now, we show that the partitioning from the consecutive cuts of the two triangles results in twelve congruent triangles (three triangles formed by each line. Each line, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/3/4e39919f572d9421d9fe01d80321554dfafdeced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;$\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />, so on so forth are parallel, forming transversals. Repeated parallel base theorems give the desired result.\n</p><p>Exactly nine of these congruent triangles form the interior of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Say these all have area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b20481843dabc7e75e548d0fa13707815f5a147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9T = 84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b29581bca5ba0bd24edae55ffee81f4fbc2ecd5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = 28/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />. Then, multiplying by the 12 triangles, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/5/9b57bd49854194a0b48af55c468e4c0574f78009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28 \\cdot 4 = \\boxed{112}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Sal_Khan\">Video Solution by Sal Khan</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Sal Khan\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l9j26EOvTYc&amp;list=PLSQl0a2vh4HCtW1EiNlfW_YoNAA38D0l4&amp;index=17\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l9j26EOvTYc&amp;list=PLSQl0a2vh4HCtW1EiNlfW_YoNAA38D0l4&amp;index=17</a> - AMBRIGGS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II\" title=\"2003 AIME II\">2003 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201319\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.070 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 537/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16144/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.456      1 -total\n 57.42%    7.152      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.93%    4.974      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3108:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201319 and revision id 284367. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}